Z||000000||Santa Cruzer||08-02-2001||07:51 PM||||I was at the light's and a kid in a grand prix GT pull's up and starts reving his motor,i saw the BIG 3800 and i thought well im gonna look like an idot but what the Hell,anyway the light changes i work my way from 1,2,d "automatic" i took him right off the straigt line I COULDEN'T BELIVE IT!,then just gained on him for about 2 cars length's he signald for me to pull over,i did and we talked for a bit he was pretty cool ,it turned out his mom had just bought him the car,ghe asked "WHAT IS THIS THING?" i said a pontiac fiero he's never seen one before "odd",and asked me how much this big v8 costs a week on gas? i said v8? nope pal it's a good ol 6,then it got better he asked my why does it have 4 pipes then?,i replied for looks i guess,he was cool but didn't know much about car's did i just get lucky with this grand prix or are our 2.8s faster then there 3800s? or maybe he just didn't know how to drive it that way?,i don't know about you guy's but whne i see 3800 it gives me the shiver's.lol<P><BR>1986 fiero se "the 86 GT style"<BR>2.8lv6,american racing rim's "15<P>------------------<BR>BlOw bIg cHuNkS oF aMeRiCaN v6 YoU rIcE CrApEr'S! <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/se.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/se.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Santa Cruzer (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||DJRice||08-02-2001||08:09 PM||||He must have forgotten to put it in gear or he has incredibly crappy reflexes...Of course, the dealer could have forgotten to install all of the spark plugs.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||p4n1c||08-02-2001||08:14 PM||||He probably couldn't push the pedal all the way to the floor because he had the seat all the way back and didn't know how to move it.  <P>There is no way, not even in a blue moon that a 2.8 can beat the 3800 unless the kid didn't know the light was green, couldn't figure out how to get it out of neutral until you were gone or couldn't reach the pedals.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||08-02-2001||08:22 PM||||Maybe the animal feet on the Toy R Us costume got tangled up in the pedals! hehe<P>Oops.. wrong guy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon12.gif"> <BR>Just teasin!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||12
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||08-02-2001||09:42 PM||||Ahh...<P>There's no way in a Blue moon a 2.8 can keep up with a 3800? Look at the weight difference in cars. I mean eventually torque would take over and he would get beat. I have beaten plenty of 3.8 series 2 powered cars , in the stop light grandprix there slugs off the line. If it were a 3.8SC I would say BS. I don't remember exact magazine times but the 3.8 series 2 cars hit 40-50 in about the same time as a 2.8 Auto<BR>Not sure about 0 to 60 times since every car varies.<P>I do know that the auto fiero has a weak gear ratio (3.33??3.35?)<P>My point of view is from a STD tranny car.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000005||p4n1c||08-02-2001||10:24 PM||||Shifting from 1 - 2 - D would not help with the takeoff against a GP GT, and I believe the GT has the 3800 II(200hp) and the GTP has the 3800 II S/C(240hp).  1st does not let you put the pedal to the floor, not in my car with a 2.8 auto at any rate.  So you lose time in switching from half pedal to full pedal between 1st and 2nd.<P>I always found I got bad takeoffs doing it that way.  I found it better to use OD or start from 2nd.  Totally skipping D, but the TH125 doesn't have OD.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'll give him the benefit of the doubt on the takeoff, but not the 2 car lengths unless the kid in the GP was a total retard.  Especially with automatics.  Standard?  Yes I can see him getting up that far if he knew how to shift well.<P>[edit]0-60 for 2.8 auto on my car(3200lbs) is 11.4 seconds with an 18 second quarter mile.  That sucks bad[/edit]<p>[This message has been edited by p4n1c (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Santa Cruzer||08-02-2001||11:00 PM||||does it help that our engine's are pushing instead of pulling?,as i said he just got the car and didn't know much but if he did i would have got smoked as i thought i was going to,: on a side note my buddy has a grand am gt a 98 with a  3.1  will i have a chance beating him with my 2.8?<P>------------------<BR>BlOw bIg cHuNkS oF aMeRiCaN v6 YoU rIcE CrApEr'S! <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/se.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierose_1986/se.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by Santa Cruzer (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||08-02-2001||11:05 PM||||18 secs in the 1/4 , , time for a major tune up , most do it in under 16.5 , most that need tune ups do it slower. <P><BR>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000008||87FieroGTx||08-03-2001||07:25 AM|||| With my 180hp 3.2 I take the 240hp? 3800's off the line all the time but at about 50 they overtake me.<P> If I'm up against a 200hp version I win almost all the time.<P> You have to remember there heavier cars and a extra 40hp over a 2.8 isn't much considering there weight, so in theory a 2.8 could keep up with the 200hp till the 3800 had some good momentum going then your toast.||||reg||1
Z||000009||p4n1c||08-03-2001||08:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>18 secs in the 1/4 , , time for a major tune up , most do it in under 16.5 , most that need tune ups do it slower. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This is a Cutlass Supreme International, not a Fiero.  The engine is to small for the weight of the car.  Granted I have popped the honeycomb out of the MAF(its been bypassed by a GM chip, the ass-o-meter says maybe 5-6hp gain) and added a K&N(.5hp at most probably).  So it does a lot better.  I need a high flow exhaust and cold air sometime later once the car is fixed up more(407,000km, she looks a little beat up).<BR><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4<BR>*Under Restoration*||||reg||1
